    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Flags low and high outliers in many numeric fields at once, within groups, by IQR, z-score or robust MAD, with bounds and optional capping.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": "Data quality",
    "tags": [
        "outliers",
        "IQR",
        "z-score",
        "MAD",
        "winsorise",
        "data quality",
        "anomalies",
        "audit",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Flags **unusually low or high values** in many numeric fields at once, optionally **within groups** (per product, category, region, machine), by a standard rule:\n\n- **IQR** (Tukey's fences): outside Q1 - k x IQR to Q3 + k x IQR, k = 1.5 by default\n- **Z-score**: more than k standard deviations from the mean, k = 3\n- **MAD** (robust z, Iglewicz and Hoaglin): 0.6745 x (value - median) / MAD above k = 3.5; not distorted by the outliers themselves\n\nGroups with fewer values than the minimum are not tested. Optionally adds **capped** (winsorised) copies of the fields, clipped to the bounds.\n\nOutputs: the rows with a Low / High / No flag per field, a count and a list; one row per outlying value with its bound, score and distance beyond the bound; and the bounds used per field and group.",
    "dependencies": "",
